WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.900
What if India's natural shield against
coastal storms suddenly disappeared?

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:07.330
This is the Sundarbans,
the world's largest mangrove forest,

00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:08.950
shared by India and Bangladesh.

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:11.600
It's home to the famous
Royal Bengal Tiger.

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:15.390
But these forests do much more
than provide a home for wildlife.

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:17.630
Their roots help stabilise shorelines,

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:21.200
trap sediments and reduce the
impact of waves and storm surges.

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:22.500
Without these mangroves,

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:25.390
coastal communities could become
more vulnerable to erosion,

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:26.810
flooding and storms.

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:31.700
An entire ecosystem would disappear, along
with a natural coastal defence system.

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:35.040
Would you protect this forest even
if it meant limiting development?

